{%- comment -%}
  Snippet: wishlist-button
  Phase 5, Stage 2. Single reusable client-only wishlist toggle, rendered
  identically everywhere it's used (product cards, PDP) — positioning is
  handled purely by the surrounding CSS context, never by a second markup
  variant. Rendered `hidden` by default; assets/wishlist.js reveals it only
  after confirming localStorage actually works, so a page with storage
  blocked/unavailable never shows an inert or broken control.

  data-label-add/-remove carry pre-translated accessible labels so
  assets/wishlist.js never hardcodes English strings — it just swaps
  aria-label using these two data attributes as aria-pressed changes.

  Params:
    product - required, a Shopify product object
{%- endcomment -%}
<button
  type="button"
  class="wishlist-button"
  data-wishlist-toggle
  data-wishlist-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-wishlist-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
  data-label-add="{{ 'wishlist.add' | t }}"
  data-label-remove="{{ 'wishlist.remove' | t }}"
  aria-pressed="false"
  aria-label="{{ 'wishlist.add' | t }}"
  hidden
>
  {%- render 'icon', icon: 'heart', size: 18 -%}
</button>
